    "title": "Wuud.",
    "lede": "Novel wooden cladding for contemporary architecture. Real wood — birch, alder, aspen, pine — modified to hold deep relief, then finished natural, translucent or painted. Developed in Finland; brought to Denmark by Beyond Rational."
  },
  "idea": {
    "eyebrow": "The process",
    "title_l1": "Wood, worked",
    "title_l2": "into relief.",
    "points": [
      {
        "num": "01",
        "title": "Embossed, not printed",
        "body": "A novel wood-modifying process presses pattern into the surface of real timber — true depth that catches light and throws shadow. Standard patterns. Or fully custom."
      },
      {
        "num": "02",
        "title": "Inside and out",
        "body": "The same modification weatherproofs the wood and adds fire retardancy — one panel language, from interior walls to building façades."
      },
      {
        "num": "03",
        "title": "From Finnish research",
        "body": "Developed out of a Business Finland & Aalto University research programme. Conscious, contemporary cladding — now available through Beyond Rational in Denmark."
